  "id": "ecological-psychology",
  "term": "ecological psychology",
  "definition": "Ecological psychology is an approach to mind and behavior that views perception and action as continuous and studies people in relation to their environments rather than as isolated individuals. It emphasizes affordances—opportunities for action in the environment—and treats cognition as embodied and situated rather than based on internal representations alone.",
